# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
from lib import *
G = 'notice'

page('ad-account-disabled-unacceptable-business-practices-help', G,
 'Unacceptable Business Practices: Ad Account Appeal Help',
 'Ad account disabled for unacceptable business practices? What the policy covers, what to check and how Unbanz prepares your appeal.',
 'Ad account disabled for unacceptable business practices?', 'Unacceptable business practices',
 'This notice is about how your business or offer looks to Meta, not a single ad. It is for advertisers who got it and need to understand what it can mean before they appeal.',
 'Meta uses this reason for ads or accounts it thinks mislead people, push deceptive offers, or cause harm to users. You can request a review in Account Quality. The appeal should show a real business, an honest offer and a landing page that matches the ad. Meta decides.',
 [('What it covers', 'Deceptive offers, hidden fees, fake urgency, misleading before and after claims and landing pages that do not match the ad.'),
  ('Check your offer', 'Read your ad and landing page as a stranger would. Look for claims you cannot prove and terms you do not show.'),
  ('Show the business', 'Registration, a clear contact page, returns and shipping terms help show that real people stand behind it.')],
 [S('What triggers this notice',
    ul(['Claims that promise results, income or health outcomes.',
        'A price or offer in the ad that is different on the landing page.',
        'Subscriptions or recurring charges that are not clearly shown before checkout.',
        'Fake countdown timers, fake stock warnings or invented reviews.',
        'A site with no contact details, no refund terms or copied product photos.'])),
  S('How to prepare before you appeal',
    ol(['Screenshot the notice, the ad and the landing page as they are today.',
        'Fix what is wrong on the site first: pricing, terms, contact page, refund and shipping policy.',
        'Remove claims you cannot back up and any fake urgency.',
        'Collect proof that the business is real: registration, invoices, supplier receipts, customer messages.',
        'Request the review once and describe what you changed.'])),
  S('How the appeal should read',
    'Say what you sell, who you sell it to and how the customer gets it. Name the changes you made to the site and the ads. Avoid arguing that the policy is unfair. A short, factual appeal with proof is what a reviewer can act on.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We go through your ads and site against Meta’s advertising standards, point out what is likely behind the notice, and prepare the appeal and supporting details. We do not advise misleading Meta or hiding anything. Read the matching guide on ' +
    A('/guides/ad-account-unacceptable-business-practices/', 'unacceptable business practices') + '.')],
 [('Is unacceptable business practices a permanent ban?', 'Not always. Meta can reverse it after a review if the business and ads meet its standards, but it can also stay in place. Meta makes the final decision.'),
  ('Can I appeal if my store really has these problems?', 'Fix them first. An appeal that shows concrete changes is stronger than one that only asks for another look.'),
  ('Does it apply to my whole business or one ad?', 'It can be either. Account Quality shows whether the ad account, the portfolio or only some ads were flagged.'),
  ('Will changing my landing page after the notice help?', 'Yes, if it fixes the real issue. Keep a record of the old and new versions to include in the appeal.')],
 ['Stores and offers that were flagged as misleading.', 'Businesses that ran urgency or scarcity tactics.', 'Advertisers with subscription or trial offers.'],
 send_extra=['The ad creative and the exact landing page link that was running.'])

page('ad-account-identity-verification-loop', G,
 'Ad Account Identity Verification Loop: What to Try',
 'Stuck in a Meta ad account identity verification loop or ID upload that keeps failing? Why it happens and what to check before you ask for help.',
 'Stuck in an identity verification loop on your ad account?', 'Identity verification loop',
 'Meta asks you to confirm your identity, you upload the ID, and the notice comes back. This page is for advertisers going around in that circle.',
 'Verification loops usually come from a mismatch: the name or date of birth on the profile does not match the ID, the photo is unreadable, or the wrong asset is being verified. Check those first, retry once with a clear photo, then ask for a review. Unbanz can look at the history with you.',
 [('Match the details', 'Name, date of birth and country on your profile must match the document you upload.'),
  ('Send a clean photo', 'Use daylight, show all four corners, no glare, no filters, and the document must not be expired.'),
  ('Verify the right asset', 'Meta can ask for verification of the profile, the ad account or the business. Each has its own flow.')],
 [S('Common reasons the loop continues',
    ul(['The profile name uses a nickname, a stylised name or a different spelling from the ID.',
        'The date of birth on the profile is different from the document.',
        'The photo is blurry, cropped or taken from a screen.',
        'The ID is not on the list accepted for your country.',
        'You are verifying the personal profile, but the request is for the business.',
        'Too many failed attempts in a short time.'])),
  S('What to try',
    ol(['Open the verification request from the notice itself rather than a saved link.',
        'Use a mobile browser or the app you normally use, and a stable connection.',
        'Check the accepted document types shown on that screen for your country.',
        'Make sure the profile name and date of birth match, and fix them if they do not. Meta limits how often you can change them.',
        'Upload one clear photo of each side and wait for the result before trying again.'])),
  S('When verification is not the real problem',
    'Sometimes the identity request is only the visible part of a larger restriction, such as a hacked profile, a payment problem or a linked disabled account. If the upload succeeds and the ad account stays restricted, look at the notice in Account Quality for the actual reason.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We check what Meta is asking you to verify, which asset it applies to and whether anything else is attached to the restriction. We never need your ID photo to be sent to us for the appeal. See also our guide on the ' +
    A('/guides/facebook-id-upload-request/', 'Facebook ID upload request') + ' and our page on ' + A('/meta-business-verification-rejected/', 'business verification rejected') + '.')],
 [('Why does Meta keep rejecting my ID?', 'The usual reasons are a name or date mismatch, an unreadable photo, an expired document or a type that is not accepted in your country.'),
  ('How many times can I try?', 'Meta limits attempts. Repeating the upload many times quickly can make it worse, so fix the cause before you retry.'),
  ('Is personal ID verification the same as business verification?', 'No. One confirms you as a person, the other confirms the business. Meta may ask for either.'),
  ('Should I send my ID to Unbanz?', 'Do not send an ID unless we ask for a specific document for a specific step. Passwords and login codes are never needed.')],
 ['Advertisers whose ID upload fails repeatedly.', 'People asked to confirm identity on a restricted ad account.', 'Business owners with a name mismatch on their profile.'])

page('ad-account-ads-rejected-repeatedly-restricted', G,
 'Ads Rejected Again and Again, Ad Account Restricted',
 'Repeated ad rejections and now a restricted ad account? How rejections add up, what to fix and how to request a review without making it worse.',
 'Repeated ad rejections led to a restricted ad account?', 'Repeated ad rejections',
 'Every rejected ad is recorded against the account. After enough of them, Meta limits or disables the ad account itself. This page is for advertisers whose rejections piled up.',
 'Repeated rejections can lead Meta to restrict the whole ad account, even if each ad seemed small. Stop resubmitting the same creative, read the exact policy named on each rejection, fix the cause, then request a review in Account Quality. Unbanz can prepare the appeal.',
 [('Stop resubmitting', 'Posting the same ad again and again adds to the record. Fix the reason first.'),
  ('Read each reason', 'Ads Manager names the policy for each rejection. They are often the same two or three.'),
  ('Appeal the account', 'Once the ads are fixed, request a review of the ad account, not just of single ads.')],
 [S('How rejections add up',
    'Meta looks at an ad account’s history, not only at the latest ad. A pattern of rejections for the same policy, or many ads sent for review in a short time, can lead to a spending limit or a restriction. Some advertisers also see delivery slow down before the notice.'),
  S('Work through the rejections',
    ol(['Export or screenshot every rejected ad with its stated reason.',
        'Group them by policy: personal attributes, misleading claims, landing page, restricted content, adult content, and so on.',
        'Fix the root cause in the creative, the text and the landing page, not just the wording of one ad.',
        'Request review on single ads only where you believe the rejection was wrong.',
        'Then request the account-level review with a short summary of what you changed.'])),
  S('Mistakes that make it worse',
    ul(['Slightly editing a rejected ad and submitting it dozens of times.',
        'Creating a new ad account to publish the rejected ads.',
        'Running the same rejected ad on a second account.',
        'Using the appeal to argue about the policy rather than showing the fix.'])),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We read the rejection history and the notice, find the pattern, and write the appeal that explains what changed. It is sent through Meta’s official review. Related reading: ' +
    A('/guides/meta-ad-rejected-request-review/', 'ad rejected: request review') + ' and ' + A('/ad-account-policy-violation-appeal/', 'policy violation appeals') + '.')],
 [('How many rejected ads lead to a restricted ad account?', 'Meta does not publish a number. The pattern, the policy involved and the account history all matter.'),
  ('Should I delete the rejected ads?', 'Do not delete them in a hurry. Keep screenshots and the stated reasons, since they show what you fixed.'),
  ('Can I appeal one ad and the account together?', 'They are separate reviews. Fix the ads first, then request the account review.'),
  ('Does a rejection always count against me?', 'A rejection is recorded, and a successful review of a wrong rejection can remove it. Repeated valid rejections are what lead to restrictions.')],
 ['Advertisers with many rejected ads on one account.', 'Teams that kept resubmitting similar creatives.', 'Businesses whose ad delivery was limited before a restriction.'])

page('ad-account-restricted-personal-attributes', G,
 'Ad Account Restricted for Personal Attributes',
 'Ads flagged for personal attributes and your ad account restricted? What Meta means, how to rewrite the ads and how to ask for a review.',
 'Ad account restricted for personal attributes?', 'Personal attributes policy',
 'Ads that speak to a person as if you know something private about them are rejected. This page is for coaches, clinics, fitness and dating-adjacent advertisers who got that notice.',
 'Meta restricts ads that assert or imply a personal attribute, such as health, finances, race or relationship status. Rewrite the ad so it talks about the offer, not the viewer, then request a review in Account Quality. Unbanz can prepare the account appeal if rejections keep adding up.',
 [('What it means', 'Wording like “Are you struggling with…” suggests you know a private fact about the reader.'),
  ('How to rewrite', 'Describe the product or service and who it is for in general terms, without addressing the person’s condition.'),
  ('Then request review', 'Fix the creative and landing page, then ask for a review of the ad account.')],
 [S('Examples of the difference',
    ul(['Flagged: “Do you have diabetes? Try this.” Safer: “A guide to meal planning.”',
        'Flagged: “Are you broke?” Safer: “Free budgeting workshop.”',
        'Flagged: “Lonely at 40?” Safer: “Meet-ups for adults in Leeds.”',
        'Flagged: before and after photos that suggest a medical result.'])),
  S('Where to check',
    'Read the ad text, the headline, the image text and the landing page. Meta checks all of them. Targeting must also respect the policy, and some sensitive categories have limited targeting options. Our guide on ' +
    A('/guides/meta-ads-health-wellness-personal-attributes/', 'health, wellness and personal attributes') + ' goes through more examples.'),
  S('Steps',
    ol(['Screenshot the rejection and the policy it names.',
        'Rewrite headlines and body text so they do not address the reader’s condition or situation.',
        'Remove before and after images and any claim of a result.',
        'Check the landing page for the same wording.',
        'Request the review, and if the account itself is restricted, request that too.'])),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We go through the ads and the landing page against the policy, show you what to change, and prepare the appeal for the account. We can also help you describe your business honestly in the appeal. See ' +
    A('/ad-account-restricted-ads-for-health-and-wellness-businesses/', 'ads for health and wellness businesses') + '.')],
 [('What counts as a personal attribute?', 'Examples are health, disability, financial status, religion, race, sexuality, age and relationship status, when the ad suggests it applies to the reader.'),
  ('Can I still advertise a clinic or a coaching offer?', 'Yes, as long as the ad describes the service without implying private facts about the viewer and follows the other policies.'),
  ('Will a rewrite alone lift the restriction?', 'It fixes future rejections. An account that is already restricted still needs a review.'),
  ('Is it allowed to use testimonials?', 'Real testimonials can be fine, but results claims and before and after images are often rejected.')],
 ['Coaches and consultants.', 'Clinics, gyms and wellness brands.', 'Anyone whose rejections name personal attributes.'])

page('ad-account-restricted-special-ad-category', G,
 'Ad Account Restricted: Special Ad Category Problems',
 'Ads rejected for housing, credit, employment or social issues? How special ad categories work and what to do when your ad account is restricted.',
 'Ad account restricted over special ad categories?', 'Special ad categories',
 'Meta applies stricter rules to ads about housing, credit, jobs and social issues. This page is for advertisers whose ads or ad account were flagged for skipping that declaration.',
 'If your ads touch housing, credit, employment or social issues, Meta expects you to declare a special ad category and accepts limited targeting. Ads that skip the declaration are rejected and can lead to a restriction. Declare correctly, fix the ads, then request a review.',
 [('Declare correctly', 'Choose the category when you create the campaign, before you publish.'),
  ('Targeting is limited', 'Age, gender, ZIP and detailed interests are restricted in these categories.'),
  ('Fix, then review', 'Update the campaign and ask for a review of the ad account if it was restricted.')],
 [S('Who needs to declare',
    ul(['Estate agents, landlords, builders and mortgage brokers.',
        'Lenders, card providers and loan brokers.',
        'Recruiters, staffing agencies and employers hiring through ads.',
        'Campaigns about elections, politics or social issues.'])),
  S('Why accounts get restricted here',
    'Ads in these areas are rejected when they run without the declaration. Repeated problems, or ads that stay live with a wrong category, can lead to restrictions. Meta has specific wording per category, and some countries add their own rules.'),
  S('What to do',
    ol(['Check which of your campaigns fall into a category, even partly.',
        'Edit the campaigns and set the right category, using the updated targeting options.',
        'Fix the ad text so it does not suggest preference for a group of people.',
        'Request review on the ad account once, with a short note on what changed.'])),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We read the rejection and the notice, help you see whether the problem is a missing declaration or something else, and prepare the appeal for the account. Read the guide to ' +
    A('/guides/meta-special-ad-categories/', 'special ad categories') + ' and our page for ' + A('/ad-account-restricted-ads-for-real-estate-agents/', 'real estate advertisers') + '.')],
 [('What is a special ad category?', 'A label you choose for ads about credit, employment, housing or social issues, elections and politics. It limits targeting and adds checks.'),
  ('Can I fix a restricted account by declaring the category now?', 'It helps with future ads. If the account is already restricted you still need a review.'),
  ('Do I need authorization to run ads about social issues?', 'In many countries yes. Meta asks for identity confirmation before political ads run.'),
  ('Does this apply outside the US?', 'Categories and rules differ by country. Read the notice for your region.')],
 ['Real estate, mortgage and lending advertisers.', 'Recruiters and employers.', 'Campaigns about social issues or elections.'])

page('ad-account-restricted-misleading-claims', G,
 'Ad Account Restricted for Misleading Claims',
 'Meta restricted your ad account for misleading or false claims? What counts, how to fix your ads and landing page and how to request a review.',
 'Ad account restricted for misleading claims?', 'Misleading claims',
 'Meta restricts accounts when ads promise things the product cannot show. This page is for advertisers whose ads or landing pages used strong claims.',
 'Misleading claims include promised results, unrealistic income, health cures and made-up reviews. If Meta flagged these, rewrite the ads and the landing page with claims you can back up, keep proof, and request a review in Account Quality. Unbanz can prepare the appeal if the account is restricted.',
 [('Spot the claim', 'Look at headline, image text, video voiceover and landing page. A claim anywhere on the path can trigger the notice.'),
  ('Replace with facts', 'Describe what the product does, with real specifics. Drop promises of results.'),
  ('Keep your proof', 'Sources, test results, certificates and real customer messages belong in your appeal.')],
 [S('Claims that are often flagged',
    ul(['Income or weight loss promises with numbers.',
        'Words like instant, miracle, cure and permanent.',
        'Fake reviews, fake media logos or invented endorsements.',
        'Before and after images that suggest a medical result.',
        'Prices or discounts that are not real.'])),
  S('How to fix it',
    ol(['Collect every ad version and the landing page as they are now.',
        'Mark each claim and ask whether you can prove it with a document.',
        'Remove or rewrite the ones you cannot.',
        'Add terms, disclaimers and contact details to the landing page.',
        'Request the review with a note about what you changed.'])),
  S('What reviewers look for',
    'Meta’s system and its reviewers look at what a normal person would take from the ad. Fine print does not rescue a headline that suggests a different message. If the landing page changes the offer, the ad is treated as misleading.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We read the notice and your ads, show you where the claims are, and prepare an appeal that describes the corrections. We do not tell you to hide anything from Meta. See also our page on ' +
    A('/ad-account-disabled-unacceptable-business-practices-help/', 'unacceptable business practices') + '.')],
 [('What does Meta consider misleading?', 'Claims that cannot be shown, results promised to the viewer, fake urgency and ads that differ from the landing page.'),
  ('Do disclaimers fix a misleading claim?', 'Rarely. If the headline suggests one thing and the fine print says another, the ad can still be rejected.'),
  ('Can testimonials cause a restriction?', 'Real ones are fine. Made-up testimonials or ones that promise results can be flagged.'),
  ('Should I wait before appealing?', 'Fix the ads first. A review before the fix usually repeats the same decision.')],
 ['E-commerce stores with strong product claims.', 'Course sellers and coaches.', 'Supplement and wellness advertisers.'])

page('ad-account-restricted-landing-page-issue', G,
 'Ad Account Restricted Because of the Landing Page',
 'Ad rejected or account restricted because of your landing page? What Meta checks, what to fix on the site and how to request a review.',
 'Ad account restricted because of the landing page?', 'Landing page problem',
 'Meta follows your ad to the page it leads to. This page is for advertisers whose site, not the ad itself, was the reason for the rejection or restriction.',
 'Meta checks that the landing page works, matches the ad and meets policy. A slow, broken, misleading or empty page can lead to rejections and eventually a restricted ad account. Fix the page first, then request a review. Unbanz can help prepare the appeal.',
 [('Page must load', 'A broken, blocked or very slow page is treated as a bad experience.'),
  ('Page must match', 'Product, price and offer must be the same as in the ad.'),
  ('Page must be real', 'Contact details, privacy policy and refund terms show a real business.')],
 [S('What Meta checks on the page',
    ul(['The page loads without errors and is not blocked for Meta’s crawler.',
        'The product or service in the ad is actually offered.',
        'Prices, terms and shipping are clear.',
        'There is a privacy policy, contact information and refund or return terms.',
        'No automatic redirects, popups that trap the visitor, or downloads without consent.'])),
  S('Fixing it',
    ol(['Open the page on mobile and on another network and check it loads quickly.',
        'Make sure your firewall or CDN is not blocking Meta’s requests.',
        'Compare the ad and the page line by line.',
        'Add the missing legal pages and a real contact route.',
        'Request review for the ad and, if needed, the account.'])),
  S('Domain and ownership',
    'If you use a new domain, verify it in business settings so Meta can tie it to your business. Changing domains right after a rejection can look like an attempt to avoid review, so explain the change. Our guide on ' +
    A('/guides/meta-domain-verification-steps/', 'domain verification') + ' covers the steps.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We go through the page with you, point out what stands out, and prepare the appeal. We do not suggest tricks that show Meta’s crawler a different page. Read more in our guide on ' +
    A('/guides/meta-ads-landing-page-rejected/', 'landing page rejections') + '.')],
 [('Can a landing page get an ad account restricted?', 'Yes. Repeated rejections because of the page can lead to a restriction on the ad account.'),
  ('Is it okay to show Meta a different page than users see?', 'No. That is the kind of behaviour that leads to a circumventing systems notice.'),
  ('Does a Shopify or Wix store need anything special?', 'Make sure policy pages exist and the checkout works. Platform defaults sometimes leave them empty.'),
  ('Do I need domain verification?', 'It is not always required, but it helps tie the domain to your business and is needed for some features.')],
 ['Stores with a new or rebuilt website.', 'Advertisers sending traffic to funnels or forms.', 'Teams that changed domain recently.'])

page('ad-account-spending-limit-stuck', G,
 'Ad Account Spending Limit Stuck or Lowered by Meta',
 'Ad account spending limit lowered or stuck and ads cannot deliver? What limits mean, what to check and when to ask for a review.',
 'Ad account spending limit stuck or lowered?', 'Spending limit problem',
 'A spend limit stops your ads from delivering even though the account looks active. This page is for advertisers who cannot raise the limit or saw it drop.',
 'Meta sets ad account spending limits based on payment history and account trust. A limit that drops or will not rise often points to billing or a trust signal. Clear any balance, check the payment method, then request a review. Unbanz can look at whether the limit is part of a restriction.',
 [('Two kinds of limit', 'A limit you set yourself, and a limit Meta applies. Only the second needs a review.'),
  ('Billing first', 'Unpaid balances and declined charges keep limits low.'),
  ('Wait for history', 'New accounts start with low limits that rise with clean payment history.')],
 [S('Where to look',
    ul(['Billing and payments: the account spending limit and the daily limit.',
        'Account Quality: whether the limit is linked to a restriction notice.',
        'Payment activity: failed or pending charges.',
        'Ads Manager notifications for limit messages.'])),
  S('Why limits stay low',
    'New ad accounts begin with small daily limits. Failed payments, many card changes or disputes keep them low. A sudden drop after a policy problem is different and is usually shown in Account Quality. Raising the limit by opening new accounts is not a fix.'),
  S('Steps',
    ol(['Check whether you set the limit yourself and remove it if so.',
        'Pay any outstanding balance and keep one reliable payment method.',
        'Look at Account Quality for a notice tied to the limit.',
        'Keep running compliant ads at modest spend so the history improves.',
        'If there is a restriction notice, request the review there.'])),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We tell you whether the limit is a normal feature of a young account or part of a restriction, and if it is the second, we prepare the appeal. Related: ' +
    A('/ad-account-restricted-payment-issue/', 'payment issue restrictions') + ' and the guide to ' + A('/guides/meta-ad-payment-declined-fix/', 'declined payments') + '.')],
 [('Why is my ad account spending limit so low?', 'New accounts and accounts with payment issues have lower limits. Meta raises them as clean payment history builds.'),
  ('Can Unbanz raise my spending limit?', 'No. We can only help with restrictions and appeals. Limits depend on Meta’s own checks.'),
  ('Is a spending limit the same as a restriction?', 'No. A restriction is a policy action. A limit can be a normal part of a new account.'),
  ('Does adding a second card raise the limit?', 'Not by itself. A reliable payment history matters more.')],
 ['Advertisers whose ads stop delivering at a low spend.', 'Teams whose limit dropped after a payment problem.', 'New accounts that cannot scale.'])

page('ad-account-disabled-after-boosting-post', G,
 'Ad Account Disabled After Boosting a Post',
 'Ad account or Page restricted right after you boosted a post? Why boosts get flagged and how to request a review.',
 'Ad account disabled after boosting a post?', 'Disabled after a boost',
 'A boost is a quick way to run an ad, and it goes through the same checks as a full campaign. This page is for people who boosted a post and then lost their ad account.',
 'Boosted posts are reviewed as ads. If the post breaks ad policy, uses a restricted topic, or the payment method fails, Meta can restrict the ad account. Check the notice, edit or remove the boosted post, then request a review. Unbanz can prepare the appeal if the review is denied.',
 [('Boosts are ads', 'They follow the same advertising standards as Ads Manager campaigns.'),
  ('Check the post', 'The caption, image, comments and the link it leads to are all part of the check.'),
  ('Check billing', 'A failed charge on a boost is one of the commonest hidden causes.')],
 [S('Why a boost leads to a restriction',
    ul(['The post uses personal attributes, health claims or banned content.',
        'The Page itself was already restricted and the boost added to it.',
        'The boost created an ad account automatically, with a card that failed.',
        'The post links to a page that does not match or does not load.',
        'The profile you boosted from was logged in from a new place.'])),
  S('What to do',
    ol(['Read the notice in Account Quality and the rejection reason on the boost.',
        'Edit or remove the boosted post if it breaks a policy.',
        'Check Billing for failed charges and clear them.',
        'Check the Page for restrictions in Page quality.',
        'Request a review for the ad account, and for the Page if it is flagged.'])),
  S('Boosts and accounts created for you',
    'When you boost without an ad account, Meta creates one in the background. If it ends up restricted, you may not know it exists. Find it in Ads Manager or Billing under the profile that boosted. Our guide on ' +
    A('/guides/meta-ad-account-restricted/', 'restricted ad accounts') + ' shows where to look.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We find the account Meta flagged, read the notice and the post history, and prepare the appeal. See also ' + A('/facebook-ad-account-restricted-help/', 'Facebook ad account restricted') + '.')],
 [('Can boosting a post get me banned?', 'A boost can lead to an ad account restriction if the post or payment breaks policy. It is not the boost itself.'),
  ('Where is the ad account created from my boost?', 'It is attached to your profile and Page. Check Ads Manager and Billing, or Account Quality, for the ID.'),
  ('Will deleting the post fix the restriction?', 'It stops further violations. The restriction itself still needs a review.'),
  ('Is my Page also at risk?', 'A Page can be limited separately. Page quality shows its status.')],
 ['Small businesses that only boost posts.', 'Creators who started paid promotion.', 'Page admins who did not know an ad account existed.'])

page('ad-account-disabled-after-advantage-plus-campaign', G,
 'Ad Account Disabled After an Advantage+ Campaign',
 'Ad account restricted after running Advantage+ shopping or automated campaigns? What can go wrong and how to request a review.',
 'Ad account disabled after Advantage+ campaigns?', 'Advantage+ campaigns',
 'Advantage+ campaigns let Meta pick placements, audiences and sometimes creative. This page is for advertisers who ran automated campaigns and then got a restriction.',
 'Automated campaigns still follow ad policy, and Meta can combine your assets in ways you did not review. A restriction after an Advantage+ campaign usually comes from creative, a landing page, or a catalog item that broke a rule. Find the item, fix it, then request a review.',
 [('Check generated variations', 'Automated text, image crops and music can create versions you never saw.'),
  ('Check the catalog', 'A product in a catalog feed can be rejected on its own and affect the whole campaign.'),
  ('Check the account', 'Account Quality shows if the account or just the campaign was flagged.')],
 [S('Where it goes wrong',
    ul(['A catalog item with a prohibited product or a misleading price.',
        'Creative enhancements that change an image in ways that suggest a claim.',
        'Broad audiences in a category where targeting is limited.',
        'A landing page that differs from the product in the feed.',
        'Rapid budget changes that look unusual for a new account.'])),
  S('What to do',
    ol(['Open the notice and the campaign with the rejection, and check each ad and catalog item.',
        'Turn off optional creative enhancements while you investigate.',
        'Remove or fix the flagged catalog items.',
        'Check the landing page and pricing against the feed.',
        'Request the review and describe what you changed.'])),
  S('Why this matters for the appeal',
    'The reviewer needs to see that you understand what was flagged. “I did not make that ad” is not an answer when the campaign was yours. Show that you now control the creative variations and that the offer is real.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We go through the campaign setup and notice, point to the likely trigger, and prepare the appeal. Our page for ' + A('/ad-account-restricted-ads-for-ecommerce-stores/', 'e-commerce advertisers') + ' covers catalog problems in more detail.')],
 [('Can Advantage+ campaigns cause a restriction?', 'They can if the creative, catalog or landing page breaks policy. The automation does not remove your responsibility for the content.'),
  ('Should I stop using Advantage+?', 'Not necessarily. Review what it generates and keep the assets clean.'),
  ('Why was only one product the problem?', 'A single catalog item can be rejected, but repeated issues can affect the whole account.'),
  ('Does Unbanz run my campaigns?', 'No. We only help with restrictions, appeals and the supporting details.')],
 ['Shops using Advantage+ shopping campaigns.', 'Teams relying on automated creative.', 'Advertisers with large catalogs.'])
